**APPROVE-WITH-NITS**

No open in-scope P0/P1. No new blocking P2 found.

Reviewed `438531ec..0e549b721f4776d514ea0b41e927e6bdd31d2a5c` against §7.5, the prior review, engineer’s fix report, and existing test/mutation logs. No files edited or suites run.

1. **P1 boot trust — FIXED.**  
   [main.cljc:637](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:637) forwards explicit `:admission`, defaulting to `{}`, independently of `:principals`. [admission_test.cljc:734](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/test/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:734) asserts declared B is refused before loading, explicitly trusted B imports, and external admission reaches the session. **Regression detection: yes.** Existing mutation logs show deriving trust from declarations and ignoring explicit admission both turn tests red. Exact fix is complete.

2. **P2 malformed allow — FIXED.**  
   [admission.cljc:191](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/src/cljc/yin/repl/admission.cljc:191) requires the exact allow key set and map conditions. Missing conditions and extra keys refuse malformed; valid nonempty conditions still refuse unsupported. [admission_test.cljc:387](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/test/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:387) checks both previously escaping shapes and no load started. **Regression detection: yes.** Removing closed-key validation turns the test red. Restoring only the `{}` fallback is correctly an equivalent mutation while key validation remains. Exact fix is complete.

3. **P3 inheritance coverage — FIXED.**  
   [admission_test.cljc:683](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/test/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:683) preinstalls an admitted module, parks a later install child, and compares the child’s inherited record with the parent’s original id/address across all four VMs. **Regression detection: yes.** Dropping admission during child inheritance produces four failures in the existing mutation log. Exact fix is complete.

4. **P3 hook once — FIXED.**  
   [link.cljc:441](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc:441) binds the legacy hook result once and reuses it. [admission_test.cljc:445](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/test/yin/repl/admission_test.cljc:445) asserts one invocation, that invocation’s refusal value, no question, and no load. **Regression detection: yes.** Reintroducing the second invocation produces two failures. Exact fix is complete; final hook removal remains AD-2’s responsibility.

5. **P3, non-blocking carryover — non-DHT admission allocation remains open.**  
   [repl.cljc:774](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:774) still allocates admission media for every session, contrary to §7.5.1. This is unchanged by the fix diff and remains a topology mismatch without an observed functional defect. **Owner: REPL engineer, AD-3. Exact fix:** supply source-kind information to session construction and allocate admission state/interpreter only for DHT compositions, retaining the pair for external DHT admission.

The **AD-3 deviation is accepted**. The explicit boot option and repeatable startup flag are a minimal policy configuration surface: strict principal parsing at [main.cljc:157](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:157), collection into `:admission :trusted` at line 596, help at line 756, and persistence through the existing `:many` machinery at [state.cljc:41](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/src/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc:41). Default trust remains own principal only, consistent with §7.5.6, §7.5.9, and the owner’s direction.

There is **no join/token trust back door**: [main.cljc:456](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:456) expands the token into declaration and following only. A fresh reader must explicitly pass `--dht-trust` to admit that publisher’s modules; later restarts may reuse explicitly saved trust. That separation is correct, not a functional usability defect. AD-3 can add `(trust)`, `(untrust)`, and `(trusted)` over the same policy; startup trust naturally remains the configured baseline preserved by reset.

The **process/head rewrites preserve their assertions** and explicitly authorize the publishers needed by their integration scenarios: [dht_head_test.cljc:96](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc:96), [dht_process_test.clj:923](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj:923), and line 1132. They exercise head/process behavior under configured policy; the new boot and CLI tests separately prove declaration alone grants no trust. The rewrites do not weaken the admission guard.

The **Node store failure is unrelated to a changed store mechanism**: neither store implementation nor [store_test.cljc:682](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad1/test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc:682) is in this diff. Existing logs confirm two failures under three-lane load, an isolated Node run with 528 tests and zero failures, and all-green changed-test lanes. This supports the reported contention/timeout diagnosis, though it cannot prove AD-1 adds zero scheduling pressure. Keep timeout/worker diagnostics with the store-test owner’s separate reliability work; it is not an AD-1 blocker.
